<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 97,053 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 97,053 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 97,053 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday compared to 94,313 tonnes in the same period on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Wednesday   March 4</p>
<p>    Export cargo		17,527	11,505</p>
<p>    Import cargo		79,526	82,808</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, three ships sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours, nine are expected to sail and 10 are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Sugar		    12,000	 Yen Men		 5/3</p>
<p>Phosphate		27,000	 Philadelphia	  5/3</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 60,000	 Miraj		   6/3</p>
<p>Petroleum products   25,000	 Chilham Castle	6/3</p>
<p>Palm oil		 12,000	 Wawasen Megah	 7/3</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     22,649	 Seram		   8/3</p>
<p>Phosphate		29,887	 Lapanto Glory	20/3</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
